{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/886334-chronicles-of-darkness-quickstart","id":886334,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness Quickstart?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-09T09:25:00-07:00","id":886334,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness Quickstart?","content":"Apologies if this has been covered elsewhere, but I was wondering if there were any plans to release a Quickstart PDF for the new Chronicles of Darkness? Are the new rules substantially different from the New World of Darkness systems?<br /> <br /> Thank you<br /> <br /> -R.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:05:02-07:00","id":886379,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, the only quickstart using the second edition rules is Vampire: the Requiem's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind?src=slider_view\" target=\"_blank\">Reap the Whirlwind</a>.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness books use the same rules as the second edition of the New World of Darkness; the &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; title is an unrelated rebranding. If you're new to the second edition of the nWoD/CofD, the original release of the second edition mortal rules as an update that references the first edition World of Darkness Rulebook, the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update?cPath=8329_20641\" target=\"_blank\">God-Machine Rules Update</a>, is still available as a free PDF, so you can browse the core mechanical differences for yourself without having to buy in first.<br /> <br /> The quick summary is: there are significant differences, primarily the Condition system and the way it ties in to experience advancement, but overall the same mechanical backbone is clearly visible. Conditions are narrative statuses that cover various kinds of situational modifiers and use them and an experience incentive to drive towards changing situations and dramatic outcomes. Flaws like being Blind, and the role of derangements as the mental and emotional consequences of trauma (expressed in broader ways less directly tied to mental disorders and illness, like being Shaken or Broken), have been folded into the Condition framework.<br /> <br /> Smaller shifts include Virtue and Vice being freeform descriptors rather than drawing from a specific list, Morality becoming the less concrete, more mental-balance-oriented Integrity, weapon ratings adding damage (on a successful roll) instead of dice, an added Social Maneuvering system for wheedling favors and information out of people over time, and an updated system for ephemeral entities that integrates the rules for ghosts and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:12:38-07:00","id":886385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/886334-chronicles-of-darkness-quickstart?p=886379#post886379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my knowledge, the only quickstart using the second edition rules is Vampire: the Requiem's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind?src=slider_view\" target=\"_blank\">Reap the Whirlwind</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/118271/Demon-The-Descent-Quickstart\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Quickstart</a> also uses the second edition rules, though I don't think it's substantively different from the Vampire one.<br /> <br /> Edit: To add to the above, the God-Machine Rules are pretty complete, but there were some minor shifts made to the new rules between the GMC's publication and the new core. Nothing fundamental, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:13:51-07:00","id":886386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> This will clear up a lot of my questions. Right around the time I was wading through the NWoD system trying to figure it out, they did the update. After a break, I'm trying to get caught up with as little fuss as possible. Thank you for your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:18:59-07:00","id":886478,"title":"","content":"Free RPG day is coming up; Onyx Path may put together something using CofD for that.","signature"